<BaseLayout title="Motor Mounts" description="LS motor mounts for the Hyundai Genesis Coupe.">
  <h1>Motor Mounts</h1>
  <p>
    Engine position sets the tone for the rest of the swap (radiator clearance, header fitment, driveshaft angle, accessory access).
    Most people use a complete kit rather than universal brackets.
  </p>

  <h2>Common Options</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Sikky</strong> — most popular complete kit. Designed to work with their oil pan and headers. <a href="https://www.sikky.com/product/hyundai-genesis-lsx-swap-kit/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Kit builder</a></li>
    <li><strong>LOJ Conversions</strong> — slotted mounts that allow more fine-tuning of engine position. <a href="https://lojkits.com/collections/hyundai-genesis-coupe-bk-engine-swap-parts" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LOJ collection</a></li>
    <li><strong>ISR Performance</strong> — cheapest mounts. Headers sit lower and are generally not recommended on powered cars. <a href="https://www.isrperformance.com/isr-performance-hyundai-genesis-ls-mount-kit/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ISR mounts</a></li>
  </ul>

